---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { appConfig } from "../app-config";

const effective = "May 19, 2026";
const updated = "May 19, 2026";

const toc = [
  { id: "principles", label: "Privacy principles" },
  { id: "collect", label: "What we collect" },
  { id: "not-collect", label: "What we do not collect" },
  { id: "use", label: "How we use data" },
  { id: "sharing", label: "Sharing & processors" },
  { id: "retention", label: "Retention" },
  { id: "rights", label: "Your rights" },
  { id: "children", label: "Children & families" },
  { id: "security", label: "Security" },
  { id: "transfers", label: "International transfers" },
  { id: "notifications", label: "Notifications" },
  { id: "cookies", label: "Cookies" },
  { id: "regions", label: "Region-specific notices" },
  { id: "automated", label: "Automated decisions" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes to this policy" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact" },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Barakah"
  description="How Barakah collects, uses, and protects your data. Privacy is amana — a trust — and we take it seriously."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  eyebrow="Legal · Privacy"
  effective={effective}
  updated={updated}
  toc={toc}
>
  <p class="lead">
    Privacy is amana — a trust. Barakah is built to support your salah, not to surveil you. This
    policy explains what we collect, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and how to control it.
  </p>

  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>The short version:</strong> we do not sell your data, we do not read the contents of
      your messages or locked apps, and we collect the minimum we need to make prayer locks work.
      Everything below is the detailed version.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section id="principles">
    <h2 data-index="01">Privacy principles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Minimum data.</strong> We collect only what the service needs to work.</li>
      <li><strong>No sale.</strong> We never sell or rent your personal data.</li>
      <li><strong>On-device by default.</strong> Sensitive settings stay on your device where they can.</li>
      <li><strong>No surveillance.</strong> We do not track movement, read messages, or scrape contacts.</li>
      <li><strong>Honest defaults.</strong> Permissions are opt-in and explained in plain language.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="collect">
    <h2 data-index="02">What we collect</h2>

    <h3>Account data</h3>
    <p>
      Email address and basic profile information when you sign up or join the waitlist. Used to
      contact you about your account and to deliver the service.
    </p>

    <h3>Device and usage data</h3>
    <p>
      Limited technical data such as device model, OS version, app version, language, time zone,
      and anonymized event counts (for example, “prayer lock triggered”). Used to keep Barakah
      stable and to fix bugs.
    </p>

    <h3>Prayer settings</h3>
    <p>
      Your chosen calculation method, locked-app selections, and prayer-window preferences. Stored
      on your device. Where you opt in to cloud sync, these are stored under your account.
    </p>

    <h3>Location</h3>
    <p>
      With your permission, your approximate location is used to calculate prayer times. You can
      grant precise or approximate location at the OS level. We do not track movement and we do not
      sell location data.
    </p>

    <h3>Payments</h3>
    <p>
      Purchases are processed by our payment provider. We receive a transaction reference, country,
      and basic billing details. We never see or store your full card number.
    </p>

    <h3>Support communications</h3>
    <p>
      When you email us, we keep your message and our reply so we can help and to keep a record of
      what was promised.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="not-collect">
    <h2 data-index="03">What we do not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The contents of your messages or any locked app.</li>
      <li>Your contacts, photos, calendar, health data, or microphone audio.</li>
      <li>Detailed movement traces or continuous background location.</li>
      <li>Browsing history outside of Barakah.</li>
      <li>Advertising identifiers for cross-app tracking.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="use">
    <h2 data-index="04">How we use data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Run the service</strong> — calculate prayer times and apply your prayer locks.</li>
      <li><strong>Support you</strong> — answer emails and resolve issues.</li>
      <li><strong>Improve Barakah</strong> — diagnose crashes and measure feature usage in aggregate.</li>
      <li><strong>Communicate</strong> — send service emails (receipts, security, important updates). Marketing emails are opt-in and unsubscribable.</li>
      <li><strong>Meet legal obligations</strong> — tax, accounting, and lawful requests.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="sharing">
    <h2 data-index="05">Sharing and processors</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal data. We share it only with the vendors that make Barakah work.
      Each is bound by a data processing agreement and limited to the purpose we engage them for.
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Category</th><th>Purpose</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Application infrastructure</td>
          <td>Backend, database, and serverless functions powering the app and website.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Authentication</td>
          <td>Sign-in, session management, and account security.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Payments</td>
          <td>Processing purchases, subscriptions, refunds, and tax compliance.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Email delivery</td>
          <td>Transactional and (opt-in) marketing email.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Analytics and crash reporting</td>
          <td>Aggregated product usage and stability monitoring.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Push notifications</td>
          <td>Delivering prayer reminders and account alerts you opt in to.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      We may disclose data when required by law or to protect the rights, safety, or property of
      Barakah, its users, or the public.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="retention">
    <h2 data-index="06">Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Account and purchase records are kept for as long as your account is active and for the
      period required by law (typically 6–7 years for financial records). Anonymized usage data may
      be retained for product analytics. You can request deletion at any time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rights">
    <h2 data-index="07">Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
      <li>Delete your data (subject to legal retention).</li>
      <li>Port your data to another service in a common format.</li>
      <li>Object to or restrict certain processing.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent at any time, without affecting prior processing.</li>
      <li>Lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any of these rights, email
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>.
      We respond within 30 days, or sooner where required by law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="children">
    <h2 data-index="08">Children and families</h2>
    <p>
      Barakah is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from
      children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us personal data, contact us and we
      will delete it. Parents and guardians who use Barakah to support a child’s salah practice
      remain responsible for managing that child’s use of the app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="security">
    <h2 data-index="09">Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use encryption in transit (TLS) and at rest where supported by our providers, vetted
      infrastructure, role-based access, and the principle of least privilege for internal access.
      No system is perfectly secure, but we work hard to protect your data and will notify you of
      material incidents as required by law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="transfers">
    <h2 data-index="10">International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Your data may be processed in countries other than your own, including the United States and
      Europe, where our providers operate. Where required, we rely on standard contractual clauses
      or equivalent safeguards.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="notifications">
    <h2 data-index="11">Notifications</h2>
    <p>
      Push notifications (prayer reminders, account alerts) are opt-in and can be turned off in
      your device settings. We send service emails (receipts, security, important updates) as part
      of operating the service. Marketing emails are opt-in and include an unsubscribe link.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="cookies">
    <h2 data-index="12">Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Our website uses a small number of cookies and similar storage for essential functionality
      (session, preferences) and privacy-respecting analytics. We honor Global Privacy Control
      signals where required. You can control cookies in your browser settings.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="regions">
    <h2 data-index="13">Region-specific notices</h2>

    <h3>European Economic Area, United Kingdom, and Switzerland</h3>
    <p>
      Where the GDPR (or UK GDPR / Swiss FADP) applies, the controller of your personal data is
      {appConfig.brand.legalName}. Legal bases include performance of contract (delivering the
      service), legitimate interests (improving Barakah, security), consent (marketing emails,
      precise location), and legal obligation (tax, accounting). You have the right to lodge a
      complaint with your supervisory authority.
    </p>

    <h3>California</h3>
    <p>
      California residents have rights under the CCPA/CPRA, including the right to know, delete,
      correct, and limit the use of sensitive personal information. We do not sell or share
      personal information for cross-context behavioral advertising.
    </p>

    <h3>Other regions</h3>
    <p>
      Where local law (such as Brazil’s LGPD, Canada’s PIPEDA, or similar) provides additional
      rights, those rights apply to you in addition to anything else stated here.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="automated">
    <h2 data-index="14">Automated decisions</h2>
    <p>
      We do not use your personal data for automated decision-making or profiling that produces
      legal or similarly significant effects on you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes">
    <h2 data-index="15">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the product evolves. Material changes will be highlighted on
      this page or communicated to you in-app or by email. The “last updated” date above always
      reflects the current version.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <h2 data-index="16">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, requests, or concerns?
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>.
    </p>
    <address>
      {appConfig.brand.legalName}<br />
      Attn: Privacy<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${appConfig.contact.email}`}>{appConfig.contact.email}</a>
    </address>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <p>
    May Allah accept your salah and grant you barakah in your time, ameen.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
